  "incident_notes": [
    "First Windows ARM64 login timed out and left no session or worker. Subsequent real login and refresh succeeded without changing TLS or network settings. A credential-free HTTP/1 GET using the approved pin and certificate validity check completed with HTTP 200; TLS handshake took about 7.65 seconds. Cause of the transient timeout was not proven.",
    "Second Windows ARM64 run authenticated and proxied traffic but switching with only one alternative favorite failed. That alternative was not among the Linux-validated successful nodes. This does not establish an OS defect or prove the candidate failure cause.",
    "Final Windows ARM64 run used a new initialized private directory, up to four dynamically measured candidates, and a harness timeout covering the existing three-candidate best-selection budget. All 49 checks passed. No node ID was hardcoded, no failure was swallowed, and no production timeout or TLS policy changed.",
    "Earlier driver SHA and enhanced driver SHA are recorded per run. Enhancement expanded the candidate pool and diagnostics; successful runs still contain 49 checks."
  ],
